          <img src={cover} alt={coverAlt} class="w-full rounded-[2rem] border border-line mt-10" />
        </figure>
    <ShareButtons title={title} url={canonical} lang={lang} extraClass="mt-8" />
      </div>

      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 py-14">
        <p class="text-ink/65 leading-relaxed mb-5">Jembrana is where Bali begins for anyone arriving by land. Ferries from Java dock at Gilimanuk around the clock, and the road east passes fishing ports, cacao groves, and one of the longest left-hand waves in Indonesia at Medewi. Further north, West Bali National Park protects some of the island's last lowland forest, home to the Bali starling and quiet snorkeling around Menjangan Island. It is a regency full of places worth visiting and products worth buying.</p>
        <p class="text-ink/65 leading-relaxed mb-5">Yet try finding those businesses with a simple Google search and most of them disappear. Surf camps without a website, producers who sell through middlemen, homestays known only by word of mouth. That visibility gap is frustrating, but it is also an opportunity: in West Bali, the competition on Google is still so thin that a modest website, set up properly, can put a small business on the first page. This guide explains what that website needs and how to get found, step by step.</p>

        <div class="bg-white border border-line rounded-3xl p-6 sm:p-8 mb-12">
    <p class="text-sm font-extrabold uppercase tracking-widest text-ink/40 mb-4">On this page</p>
    <ol class="list-decimal pl-5 space-y-2.5 text-ink/70 leading-relaxed">
      <li><a href="#west-bali-businesses-google" class="font-semibold text-brand hover:underline">Why West Bali Businesses Are Hard to Find on Google Today</a></li>
      <li><a href="#medewi-surf-camp-website" class="font-semibold text-brand hover:underline">What a Medewi Surf Camp Website Needs to Win Guests</a></li>
      <li><a href="#jembrana-producers-website" class="font-semibold text-brand hover:underline">What Jembrana Producers Need from a Website to Sell Beyond Bali</a></li>
      <li><a href="#local-seo-jembrana" class="font-semibold text-brand hover:underline">Local SEO Basics for Jembrana: Maps, Reviews, and Consistent Details</a></li>
      <li><a href="#jembrana-30-day-plan" class="font-semibold text-brand hover:underline">A Simple 30 Day Plan to Get Your Jembrana Business Found Online</a></li>
      <li><a href="#west-bali-deserves-to-be-found" class="font-semibold text-brand hover:underline">The West Deserves to Be Found: A Website Is the First Step</a></li>
    </ol>
  </div>
  <h2 id="west-bali-businesses-google" class="text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-tight mt-2 mb-5 scroll-mt-32">Why West Bali Businesses Are Hard to Find on Google Today</h2>
        <p class="text-ink/65 leading-relaxed mb-5">The first reason is simple: many Jembrana businesses have no official website at all. Their information lives scattered across Instagram posts, a Facebook page last updated years ago, and a phone number passed between travelers. Google can index social posts, but it trusts a proper website far more when deciding what to show for searches like "surf camp Medewi" or "Bali cacao supplier".</p>
        <p class="text-ink/65 leading-relaxed mb-5">The second reason is geography. Bali's south, from Canggu to Uluwatu, is saturated with businesses that have invested in websites and SEO for a decade, so search results skew heavily toward them. Meanwhile, travelers planning a west coast trip do almost everything from their phones: checking the surf forecast, comparing rooms, figuring out the drive from Gilimanuk. If your business does not appear in that moment of planning, the booking goes somewhere else, often to a platform that takes a commission. The good news is that searches with "Medewi" or "Jembrana" in them have far fewer competitors, so showing up there is genuinely achievable.</p>

        <h2 id="medewi-surf-camp-website" class="text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-tight mt-14 mb-5 scroll-mt-32">What a Medewi Surf Camp Website Needs to Win Guests</h2>
        <p class="text-ink/65 leading-relaxed mb-5">A surf camp sells an experience, but guests book based on clear, practical information. Your website should answer the questions every surfer asks before committing to the trip west:</p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2.5 text-ink/65 leading-relaxed mb-6">
          <li><strong>The wave, explained honestly.</strong> Describe Medewi's long left-hander as it really is: the best swell directions, which tides suit beginners and which suit experienced surfers, and how conditions change between the dry and wet seasons. Honest detail builds trust and attracts the guests who will actually enjoy your break.</li>
          <li><strong>Rooms and rates.</strong> Photos of every room type with the nightly rate and what is included, so guests do not have to message three camps just to compare basics.</li>
          <li><strong>Board rental and lessons, with prices.</strong> List your board quiver by size, rental rates per day, and lesson packages with instructor ratios. Surfers traveling light decide fast when this is clear.</li>
          <li><strong>Transfer information.</strong> How to reach you from Ngurah Rai Airport and from Gilimanuk harbor, how long each drive takes, and whether you offer pickups. This page alone removes the biggest hesitation about staying in the west.</li>
          <li><strong>Food and daily rhythm.</strong> A small gallery of meals, the warung nearby, yoga deck, and what a typical day looks like. Guests staying a week or more want to picture their routine.</li>
          <li><strong>A WhatsApp booking button.</strong> One tap should open a chat with a pre-filled message. Direct bookings mean no platform commission and a personal connection before the guest even arrives.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 id="jembrana-producers-website" class="text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-tight mt-14 mb-5 scroll-mt-32">What Jembrana Producers Need from a Website to Sell Beyond Bali</h2>
        <p class="text-ink/65 leading-relaxed mb-5">Jembrana's producers, from cacao farmers around Melaya to seafood processors at Pengambengan, face a different problem: buyers outside Bali cannot find them, so the harvest moves through layers of middlemen. A straightforward company website changes who gets to contact you first:</p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2.5 text-ink/65 leading-relaxed mb-6">
          <li><strong>A product catalog with grades and packaging.</strong> For cacao, coffee, or dried seafood, list each product with its grade, moisture or processing standard where relevant, minimum order, and available packaging sizes. Buyers think in specifications, so give them specifications.</li>
          <li><strong>Your production story and capacity.</strong> Where the raw material comes from, how it is fermented, dried, or processed, and roughly how much you can supply per month. This is what separates a producer from an anonymous trader in a buyer's eyes.</li>
          <li><strong>A wholesale and reseller contact.</strong> A dedicated page or section for trade inquiries, with a WhatsApp number answered by someone who can discuss volume and pricing.</li>
          <li><strong>Certifications or lab results, only if you truly have them.</strong> If your products have been lab tested or your group holds a certification, publish it with the document visible. If not, leave this section out entirely; honest absence beats borrowed logos.</li>
          <li><strong>Delivery coverage beyond Bali.</strong> State clearly which regions you can ship to, through which couriers or cargo services, and typical lead times. A buyer in Surabaya or Jakarta needs this before they will start a conversation.</li>
        </ul>

        <div class="bg-brand text-white rounded-[2rem] p-8 sm:p-10 my-14">
      <h3 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-tight">Your West Bali business deserves to be found</h3>
      <p class="text-white/85 leading-relaxed mt-3 mb-7">Get a website that puts your surf camp, rooms, or products on Google where your guests actually look. Packages start from just a few hundred thousand rupiah, and the consultation is free.</p>
      <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3">
