    <h2 id="local-seo-jembrana" class="text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-tight mt-14 mb-5 scroll-mt-32">Local SEO Basics for Jembrana: Maps, Reviews, and Consistent Details</h2>
        <p class="text-ink/65 leading-relaxed mb-5">A website alone is not enough; Google also needs to believe your business is real and local. Start with a Google Business Profile and claim it properly. Use one consistent business name, address, and phone number everywhere: on your website, your Maps listing, and your social profiles. Inconsistent details, such as two different phone numbers, quietly weaken your ranking.</p>
        <p class="text-ink/65 leading-relaxed mb-5">Check that your map pin sits exactly on your location, not at the village center or the main road. In rural areas a misplaced pin can send guests to the wrong hamlet entirely. Then work on reviews: ask happy guests and buyers to leave one, and reply to every review you receive, good or bad, briefly and politely. Finally, add fresh photos to your profile regularly, real photos of the rooms, the harvest, the boats, the team. Profiles with recent photos look alive to both Google and the humans browsing them.</p>

        <h2 id="jembrana-30-day-plan" class="text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-tight mt-14 mb-5 scroll-mt-32">A Simple 30 Day Plan to Get Your Jembrana Business Found Online</h2>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold mt-9 mb-3">Week 1: Claim your place on the map</h3>
        <p class="text-ink/65 leading-relaxed mb-5">Create or claim your Google Business Profile, fix the pin, add your hours, phone number, and a first batch of ten good photos. This costs nothing and is the single fastest visibility win available to you.</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold mt-9 mb-3">Week 2: Launch a simple website</h3>
        <p class="text-ink/65 leading-relaxed mb-5">Put up a clean website with the pages described above: your offer, your prices or catalog, how to reach you, and a WhatsApp button. Simple and accurate beats elaborate and half finished. Make sure the name, address, and phone number match your Maps profile exactly.</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold mt-9 mb-3">Week 3: Publish two helpful pages</h3>
        <p class="text-ink/65 leading-relaxed mb-5">Add two pages that answer real questions your customers ask. A surf camp might write a guide to Medewi's seasons and tides, or how to get from Gilimanuk to Medewi. A producer might write about how their cacao is fermented, or the difference between their product grades. These pages are what Google shows to people who are researching, not just buying.</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold mt-9 mb-3">Week 4: Start the review habit</h3>
        <p class="text-ink/65 leading-relaxed mb-5">Ask every happy guest or buyer, in person and with a short link, to leave a review. Reply to each one. From here on, this is not a project but a habit, a few minutes a week that compounds month after month.</p>

        <h2 id="west-bali-deserves-to-be-found" class="text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-tight mt-14 mb-5 scroll-mt-32">The West Deserves to Be Found: A Website Is the First Step</h2>
        <p class="text-ink/65 leading-relaxed mb-5">West Bali does not lack quality; it lacks visibility. The surf is world class, the cacao is excellent, and the road from Gilimanuk brings thousands of potential customers past your door every week. A clear website and a cared-for Maps profile are how those people find you instead of scrolling past. If you would like to see what it costs, our <a href="/en/harga/" class="font-semibold text-brand hover:underline">transparent pricing page</a> lists every package in plain sight, and our <a href="/jasa-pembuatan-website-di-jembrana/" class="font-semibold text-brand hover:underline">web design service for Jembrana</a> page explains how we work with businesses across the regency. The west deserves to be found, and getting found is a solvable problem.</p>
      </div>

